# Added: 2026-04-07 (worker-service trivy gate failure on staging push)
# Both unfixed in Debian 13.4 linux-libc-dev 6.12.74-2; container userspace
# headers only — runtime uses host kernel. Review by 2026-05-07.
CVE-2026-23401
CVE-2026-31408

# Added: 2026-04-09 (worker-service trivy gate failure — 4th consecutive)
# linux-libc-dev 6.12.74-2, status: affected (no Debian fix available).
# kernel: net: atm: fix crash due to unvalidated vcc pointer.
# Impact: None — container userspace headers only; containers use host kernel,
# and the atm (Asynchronous Transfer Mode) networking subsystem is not used.
# Verified locally: `trivy image --ignorefile .trivyignore meshant-worker-trivy-test`
# returns Total: 0 after this entry.
# Review by: 2026-05-09
CVE-2026-31411

# Added: 2026-04-15 (worker-service trivy gate failure — Phase 224/225 deploy)
# Both unfixed in Debian linux-libc-dev 6.12.74-2, status: affected.
# CVE-2026-31414 — kernel: netfilter: nf_conntrack_expect: use expect->helper.
# CVE-2026-31419 — kernel: Use-after-free in bonding driver.
# Impact: None — container userspace headers only; containers use host kernel,
# and neither nf_conntrack_expect nor the bonding driver runs in our workloads.
# Review by: 2026-05-15
CVE-2026-31414
CVE-2026-31419

# Added: 2026-04-15 (datacontract-service trivy gate — Phase 224/225 deploy)
# CVE-2026-6100 — Python: use-after-free in decompression (libpython3.13
# 3.13.5-2), status: affected (no Debian fix yet). Hits libpython3.13-minimal,
# libpython3.13-stdlib, python3.13, python3.13-minimal in the
# datacontract-service base image.
# Impact: Low — datacontract-service does not decompress untrusted user input
# (it validates JSON/YAML contract specs, which the decompression code path
# does not exercise). API ingress is through Spring / JAX-RS, not tarfile /
# zipfile / lzma consumers. Containers will pick up the patch automatically
# when Debian ships a fixed libpython3.13-*.
# Review by: 2026-05-15
CVE-2026-6100

# Added: 2026-04-23 (worker-service trivy gate — run 24855818894)
# Forty kernel CVEs published today in the Debian vulndb against
# linux-libc-dev 6.12.74-2 (Debian 13.4 "Trixie"). All status: affected,
# no fixed version available. Same class as every other linux-libc-dev
# entry in this file: container userspace headers only — runtime uses
# the host kernel, the package's kernel code is never executed.
# Verified: all 40 entries come from the SAME package (linux-libc-dev)
# via `gh run view 24855818894 --log-failed | grep -E 'linux-libc'`.
# Subsystems touched by the CVE titles include: perf, netfs, netfilter,
# sched/core, drm, sound, vfs, bpf, io_uring, fs/ocfs2 — none of which
# are invoked from our container workloads (the scan flags the headers
# as vulnerable because Trivy doesn't distinguish between headers and
# running kernel).
# Review by: 2026-05-23 — expect most to have Debian fixes by then.
#
# Added: 2026-04-24 (worker-service trivy gate — run 24867604444)
# Another 8 kernel CVEs flagged on linux-libc-dev 6.12.74-2. Same class
# as the 40 immediately below. These fall in the CVE-2026-233xx range
# (between existing suppressions 23102..23392) — disclosed between the
# 2026-04-03 and 2026-04-23 vulndb updates and missed by both prior
# passes. All status=affected, no Debian fix available, kernel headers
# only (no runtime exposure in container workloads).
# Review by: 2026-05-24.
